/-!
# Genus lower bound for the level-N modular function field

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.LevelN.twelve_mul_add_mul_index_le_genusFF`
(`4d8ea939-d6e9-53f2-b8e0-64b3279c447c`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `1cab8fef-a829-5ce1-ab34-b1401ca56088`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a natural number, nonzero, with $2 \le N$, and let $K$ be a field carrying an algebra
structure over $\mathbb{C}$ and over [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), these being compatible (a scalar tower), and
such that $K$ is a fraction field of [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28). Here [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) is the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of the algebra of
functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ on the upper half-plane generated by the set consisting of the
analytic $j$-function `jAnalytic` together with all Fricke functions `fricke N v` for $v :
\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{Z}/N$ with $v \neq 0$; thus $K$ is a model of the field of modular
functions of level $N$. Write $\mu_N$ for the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup
generated by the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(N)$ together with the integer powers of $-1$,
and $g =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF ℂ K`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions.html#L145), the
$\mathbb{C}$-dimension of the space $H^1$ attached to the zero divisor in the group of divisors
$\mathrm{Place}\,\mathbb{C}\,K \to_{\mathrm{f}} \mathbb{Z}$ of the function field $K/\mathbb{C}$.
The assertion is the inequality of natural numbers $$12N + N\mu_N \le 12N\,g + 6\mu_N,$$
equivalently $g \ge 1 + \mu_N(N-6)/(12N)$.

This is the classical genus formula for the modular curve $X(N)$, $N \ge 2$, in the form of the
inequality $g \ge 1 + \mu_N(N-6)/(12N)$ obtained from the ramification of $K/\mathbb{C}(j)$ above $j
= 0, 1728, \infty$ and the Riemann–Hurwitz bound, with $g$ taken in the adelic (function-field)
sense. It is used to bound from below the dimension of the space of cusp forms for $\Gamma(N)$, in
[`ModularCurve.twelve_mul_add_mul_index_le_finrank_cuspForm_Gamma`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.twelve_mul_add_mul_index_le_finrank_cuspForm_Gamma).

